Market Challenges
Scaling cylindrical battery production to meet commercial vehicle demand remains a major challenge. Manufacturing large-format cells requires specialized equipment, strict process controls, and consistent production yields. Delays in factory commissioning and qualification can affect supply availability.

The absence of standardized cell formats and battery-pack architectures also complicates integration. Truck manufacturers must evaluate compatibility, maintenance requirements, thermal performance, and safety before adopting new battery technologies.

Market Restraints
Raw material price volatility can affect battery production costs and supplier profitability. Lithium, nickel, and other battery materials are exposed to changes in mining capacity, processing costs, and international supply conditions.

Charging infrastructure limitations also restrict electric truck deployment, particularly for long-distance freight operations. High-power charging facilities require substantial investment, while battery thermal management and replacement complexity can increase the total cost of ownership.

